cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "CCID-Epigenome: evidence-convergent prioritization of partial-reprogramming CpGs"
abstract: >-
  A sequential, evidence-convergent workflow that prioritizes DNA methylation
  CpGs associated with maturation-phase transient reprogramming (MPTR) as
  candidate loci for direction-specific epigenome-editing experiments, and
  evaluates whether their methylation directions oppose independent cellular
  aging trajectories. Includes donor-robustness analysis, perturbation-network
  evidence, regulatory annotation, score-layer sensitivity analysis, and
  orthogonal validation against independent transient-reprogramming,
  replicative-aging and multidonor fibroblast-lifespan datasets.
type: software
version: "0.9.1"
date-released: "2026-10-29"
